# Git ↔ Jira branches

When you pick a Jira issue, the branch prefix follows the issue type and the **board key** — not a hardcoded `INK`.

| Jira type | Prefix |
|---|---|
| Bug | `bug/` |
| Feature, Story, Task, Epic | `feature/` |

Pattern: `{prefix}{PROJECT}-{n}`

Examples:

- INK Feature INK-26 → `feature/INK-26`
- INK Bug INK-53 → `bug/INK-53`
- CMS Feature CMS-35 → `feature/CMS-35`
- FORGE Bug FORGE-82 → `bug/FORGE-82`

`PROJECT` is the Jira project key (`INK`, `CMS`, `FORGE`, `CTX`). Do not use Linear auto slugs (`yaghobieh/gat-…`).

## Integration

Ink CMS work currently lives on `feature/1.1.7-cms-real`. Ticket branches PR into that branch (or `release/{version}` when the sprint branch exists). Do not merge CMS WIP into `main` mid-sprint.
